    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Luis Arraez** (69.53) and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) headline our active roster as the strongest individual plays. **Arraez** benefits immensely from a favorable matchup against Grayson Rodriguez (5.27 xERA) and wind conditions that provide a modest boost to his output from the leadoff spot. Meanwhile, **Dylan Beavers** finds himself in an ideal situation against the struggling G. Holmes, capitalizing on a 16% park factor advantage and strong SP skill metrics. **Taylor Ward** (69.25) remains a pillar in our utility slot, maintaining high efficiency despite a slight platoon dip, largely sustained by the same favorable environment supporting **Dylan Beavers**. While **Jung Hoo Lee** (67.17) carries a strong score, his upside is slightly capped by the elite catching framing of the opponent, though his platoon edge against Rodriguez keeps him firmly in the green.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Jonathan Aranda** (48.26), who narrowly missed the cut. While **Aranda** holds a respectable projection, his negative platoon adjustment against the left-handed Cantillo combined with suboptimal park factors made him less efficient than **Gavin Sheets** (52.31) or **Kyle Karros** (49.56). We are monitoring the 41% rain risk involving **Masyn Winn**, whose moderate score of 59.67 is contingent on playability; should a delay or postponement occur, we are prepared to pivot to **Tyler Freeman** or **Gleyber Torres**, who were both heavily considered but ultimately benched due to lower relative ceiling outcomes today. \n\nStrategic attention must be paid to **Lawrence Butler** (65.97), whose robust score is driven by a massive 13% dynamic platoon boost against Matthews, effectively neutralizing the drag of his #8 batting position. Conversely, **Bryce Harper** (53.93) is our most aggressive start against a tough arm in Schlittler; despite the lower score compared to our leadoff hitters, his floor remains too high to justify benching. With stolen bases serving as our primary scarcity constraint, we are banking on the high-contact approach of **Luis Arraez** and the situational utility of our depth to maintain our category lead.",
